title: temporarily disable sleep
pid: 56828444-7dd4-4417-91f4-8d2c68ba6604
body: |2-
  SURPRISING. Read this whole thing.

  In a shell, run this:
    systemd-inhibit --what=sleep:idle --mode=block bash
  That 'opens a new shell' (doesn't look different)
  which, for as long as it's running, prevents suspension.
  Running 'exit' (or Ctrl-D) exits it (again doesn't look different),
  whenceforth suspension is normal.
